stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> DISCONNECTED

    DISCONNECTED --> CONNECTING : connect()
    CONNECTING --> CONNECTED : connection_succeeds
    CONNECTING --> RECONNECTING : connection_fails
    CONNECTING --> RECONNECTING : connection_timeout
    CONNECTING --> DISCONNECTED : disconnect()
    CONNECTING --> FAILED : max_retries_exhausted

    CONNECTED --> DISCONNECTED : disconnect()

    RECONNECTING --> CONNECTING : backoff_elapsed
    RECONNECTING --> CONNECTED : connection_succeeds (next iteration)
    RECONNECTING --> RECONNECTING : connection_fails
    RECONNECTING --> RECONNECTING : connection_timeout
    RECONNECTING --> DISCONNECTED : disconnect()
    RECONNECTING --> FAILED : max_retries_exhausted

    FAILED --> CONNECTING : connect() [retry_count NOT reset → stuck]
    FAILED --> DISCONNECTED : disconnect() [violates R-05 permanent]

    note right of FAILED
        Q-02: R-05 says FAILED is permanent.
        disconnect() transitions to DISCONNECTED
        without checking FAILED.
        connect() from ex-FAILED starts
        _connect_loop which exits immediately
        because retry_count >= max_retries,
        leaving state stuck in CONNECTING.
    end note
